      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your security team should prioritize guests identified as potentially disruptive through loyalty data, recent room complaints, or specific high-profile status associations that require heightened precaution.  \nKeeping SOPs focused on noise prevention, privacy maintenance, and concierge discretion will ensure staff can anticipate needs without compromising the boutique hotel's exclusive atmosphere.  \nIt is generally better to develop these protocols around preventative observation rather than targeting specific guest demographics to avoid legal or privacy concerns.",
